{
 "id": "M15",
 "kind": "echarts",
 "title": "No hard backdoor is both stealthy and seriously harmful",
 "section": "appendix",
 "order": 123,
 "caption": "The 51 hardest backdoors, each rated by hand on two axes: how obviously planted the code looks to a reviewer, and how much damage the bug does when its trigger fires. Cells hold counts. The stealthy and severe block, top right, is empty.",
 "notes": [
  "23 are stealthy and low stakes, 23 are visible but minor, 5 are visible and severe, and 0 are stealthy and severe. The quadrant that would worry you most is the one with nothing in it.",
  "That emptiness is about this set, not about backdoors in general. These 51 were chosen because the monitors failed on them, so the sample is selected on being hard to catch.",
  "Hand ratings, not measurements. Each backdoor was rated twice and disagreements adjudicated: 33 agreed first time, 18 needed adjudication, and 1 is still marked medium confidence. The per-backdoor reasons are in the CSV.",
  "An impact of 4 never occurs, so that column is empty in both directions. The scale is kept at five points rather than redrawn to fit the data.",
  "Scores for the same backdoors live in opus-hard51-scores.csv and join on sample_id. This table deliberately does not repeat them."
 ],
